{"name":"Golden Goose","hex":"#ffd34e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden goose","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something that generates much profit or gives great advantages."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden_goose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Goose (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Goose (GG) is an Italian luxury fashion company specialized in footwear and apparel headquartered in Milan, Italy, by fashion designers Gallo and Rinaldo Founded in 2000 in Marghera near Venice, the brand is best known for its handcrafted sneakers with a distinctive distressed, vintage look. Its most recognizable model, the Super-Star, introduced in 2007, features a stylized star logo with one point deliberately shortened or obscured, reflecting the company's imperfect aesthetic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Golden_Goose_Walton_Street_London_April_2022.jpg/330px-Golden_Goose_Walton_Street_London_April_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Goose_(company)","wikidata":"Q28224724"},{"title":"The Golden Goose","blocks":[{"text":"\"The Golden Goose\" is a fairy tale collected by the Brothers Grimm."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Simpleton_finds_The_Golden_Goose_-_Project_Gutenberg_eText_15661.jpg/330px-Simpleton_finds_The_Golden_Goose_-_Project_Gutenberg_eText_15661.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Golden_Goose","wikidata":"Q652607"},{"title":"Goose","blocks":[{"text":"A goose is a bird of any of several waterfowl species in the family Anatidae. This group comprises the genera Anser and Branta. Some members of the Tadorninae subfamily are commonly called geese, but are not considered \"true geese\" taxonomically. More distantly related members of the family Anatidae are swans, most 